---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Psychiatric Medication Management in Idaho | MWRS"
    description="Medication support for anxiety, depression, ADHD, and related concerns. In-person visits in Coeur d’Alene and Ponderay, with telehealth across Idaho."
>
    <main class="subpage">
        <section class="subpage-hero">
            <div class="subpage-hero-inner">
                <h1>Medication Management</h1>
                <p>
                    MWRS offers thoughtful psychiatric medication management for
                    adults and teens dealing with anxiety, depression, ADHD, and
                    related concerns. Our psychiatric nurse practitioners
                    (PMHNPs) provide careful, collaborative care with in-person
                    visits in Coeur d’Alene and Ponderay, plus telehealth across
                    Idaho.
                </p>
                <a href="/contact-us#medication" class="subpage-btn">
                    Request a medication appointment
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="subpage-section">
            <div class="subpage-inner">
                <h2>When medication may help</h2>
                <p>
                    Medication is not the right fit for everyone, but it can be
                    a helpful part of care when symptoms feel persistent,
                    disruptive, or hard to manage through counseling alone.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Some clients reach out because anxiety feels constant,
                    depression is wearing them down, or focus and attention
                    issues are affecting work, school, or daily life. Others
                    simply want to talk through options with a prescriber and
                    decide what makes sense.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Our approach is thoughtful and collaborative. We take time
                    to understand what has been going on, answer questions
                    clearly, and consider whether medication fits your goals,
                    preferences, and overall care.
                </p>

                <h3>Medication support may be worth considering for:</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Anxiety that feels difficult to settle</li>
                    <li>Depression that is affecting daily life</li>
                    <li>
                        ADHD symptoms such as focus, organization, or
                        follow-through
                    </li>
                    <li>Mood-related concerns that need further evaluation</li>
                    <li>
                        Situations where counseling alone has not felt like
                        enough
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="subpage-section subpage-section-light">
            <div class="subpage-inner">
                <h2>What to expect</h2>
                <p>
                    The first appointment is a chance to talk through what has
                    been going on, ask questions, and decide whether medication
                    support makes sense for you. It is not a rushed or
                    one-size-fits-all process.
                </p>

                <h3>At your first visit, we may talk about:</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Your current symptoms and how long they have been
                        affecting you
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Past counseling, medication, or other treatment history
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Sleep, stress, focus, mood, and day-to-day functioning
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Your goals, preferences, and any concerns about
                        medication
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <p>
                    If medication seems like a good fit, your prescriber can
                    talk through options, next steps, and follow-up care. If it
                    does not, that is okay too. The goal is to find an approach
                    that fits your needs.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="subpage-section">
            <div class="subpage-inner">
                <h2>Locations and availability</h2>
                <p>
                    We offer medication management for adults and teens across
                    Idaho, with both in-person and telehealth options.
                </p>

                <h3>In-person appointments</h3>
                <p>Available in Coeur d’Alene and Ponderay.</p>

                <h3>Telehealth</h3>
                <p>
                    Available anywhere in Idaho through a secure video platform.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Some clients prefer in-person visits, while others choose
                    telehealth or a mix of both depending on their schedule and
                    needs.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="faq-list-section">
            <div class="faq-list-inner">
                <h2 class="faq-section-title">Common questions</h2>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        Do I have to take medication if I schedule an
                        appointment?
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            No. The first visit is a conversation. You and your
                            provider will talk through your symptoms, history,
                            and goals, and decide together whether medication
                            makes sense.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        Can I do both counseling and medication management?
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            Yes. Many clients use both. Medication can support
                            symptom relief, while counseling helps address
                            patterns, relationships, and long-term change.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        How often are follow-up appointments?
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            This depends on your situation. Some clients meet
                            more frequently at the beginning and then space
                            visits out once things are stable.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        Do you offer telehealth?
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            Yes. We offer secure telehealth appointments for
                            clients anywhere in Idaho, along with in-person
                            visits in Coeur d’Alene and Ponderay.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>

                <details class="faq-item">
                    <summary class="faq-question">
                        What conditions do you treat?
                    </summary>
                    <div class="faq-answer">
                        <p>
                            We commonly help with anxiety, depression, ADHD, and
                            related concerns, but each situation is unique. The
                            first step is a conversation to understand what you
                            are dealing with.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </details>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="subpage-section subpage-cta">
            <div class="subpage-inner">
                <h2>Ready to talk through your options?</h2>
                <p>
                    Whether you are looking for support with anxiety,
                    depression, ADHD, or something less clear-cut, we can help
                    you decide whether medication care makes sense for your
                    situation.
                </p>
                <a href="/contact-us#medication" class="subpage-btn">
                    Request a medication appointment
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>

    <style>
        .subpage {
            background: #f9fafb;
            min-height: 100vh;
        }

        .subpage-hero {
            padding: 10rem 1.5rem 3rem;
            background-color: #fbfbf9;
            background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.png");
            background-repeat: repeat;
            background-size: 420px 420px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        }

        .subpage-hero-inner {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .subpage-hero h1 {
            font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
            font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
            letter-spacing: 0.16em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            color: #111827;
        }

        .subpage-hero p {
            margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
            font-size: 1rem;
            line-height: 1.8;
            color: #4b5563;
        }

        /* CSS */
        .subpage-btn {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 0.85rem 1.9rem;
            border-radius: 999px;
            border: 1px solid #0f172a;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.14em;
            text-decoration: none;
            background: #ffffff;
            color: #0f172a;
            font-weight: 600; /* ← add this */
            box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);
            transition:
                background 0.15s ease,
                color 0.15s ease,
                box-shadow 0.15s ease,
                transform 0.15s ease;
        }

        .subpage-btn:hover {
            background: #0f172a;
            color: #ffffff;
            transform: translateY(-1px);
            box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.2);
        }
        .subpage-section {
            padding: 3rem 1.5rem 3.2rem;
            background: #e5e9f3;
            background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.png");
            background-repeat: repeat;
            background-size: 420px 420px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        }

        .subpage-inner {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .subpage-section h2 {
            font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            letter-spacing: 0.18em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            color: #111827;
        }

        .subpage-section h3 {
            margin: 1.25rem 0 0.4rem;
            margin-top: 1.5rem;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            letter-spacing: 0.08em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            color: #111827;
        }

        .subpage-section p {
            margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
            font-size: 0.96rem;
            line-height: 1.8;
            color: #4b5563;
        }

        .subpage-section ul {
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
            padding-left: 1.1rem;
            font-size: 0.95rem;
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: #4b5563;
        }

        .subpage-section li + li {
            margin-top: 0.2rem;
        }
        .subpage-section-light {
            background: #fbfbf9;
        }
        .subpage-cta {
            background: #fbfbf9;
            text-align: center;
            border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
        }

        .subpage-cta p {
            max-width: 620px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
        }
        .faq-list-section {
            padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
            background: #e5e9f3;
            background-image: url("/images/paper-texture.png");
            background-repeat: repeat;
            background-size: 420px 420px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        }

        .faq-list-inner {
            max-width: 900px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 1.3rem;
        }

        .faq-section-title {
            font-family: "Belleza", sans-serif;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            letter-spacing: 0.18em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
            color: #111827;
        }

        .faq-item {
            border-radius: 20px;
            background: #ffffff;
            border: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
            box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
            padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem;
        }

        .faq-item summary {
            list-style: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
            display: none;
        }

        .faq-question {
            font-size: 0.98rem;
            font-weight: 500;
            color: #111827;
            margin: 0;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.75rem;
        }

        .faq-item summary::after {
            content: "+";
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            color: #6b7280;
            flex-shrink: 0;
            transition:
                transform 0.15s ease,
                color 0.15s ease;
        }

        .faq-item[open] summary::after {
            content: "–";
            color: #111827;
        }

        .faq-answer {
            margin-top: 0.6rem;
            font-size: 0.94rem;
            line-height: 1.7;
            color: #4b5563;
        }

        .faq-answer p {
            margin: 0;
        }
    </style>
</Layout>
